# Analysis plan: sample-pca

Status: DRAFT

This plan awaits user review. Nothing executes until the user approves it and the stage 03
approval helper records that approval.

## Goal
Perform a PCA of the RNA-seq samples from gene counts, coloured by condition.
Display PC1 versus PC2 with sample labels and explained variance to describe sample relationships.

## Inputs
Resolve both inputs again at execution time using `_system/resolve_artifact.py --project
<project> --assay rnaseq_bulk --consumes counts_gene design`; stop if either cannot resolve.
Paths below are relative to the project and reflect current resolution. Inputs are read-only.

| Artifact type | Resolved from | Path |
|---|---|---|
| counts_gene | 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper, native | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets, native | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

Current design: A1, A2, A3 are untreated; B1, B2, B3 are treated. The count matrix
contains gene_id and gene_name annotation columns followed by sample columns.

## Method
1. After approval, write `scripts/sample_pca.py` and `scripts/submit.sh` inside this analysis.
   Run all data processing and plotting in batch using Python in `gars-bio`, with pandas,
   NumPy and Matplotlib from the existing environment. Use NumPy SVD for PCA; install nothing.
2. Read the resolved TSV counts and CSV design. Use gene_id as the unique gene identifier;
   exclude gene_name from numeric calculations. Require unique nonempty sample IDs, nonempty
   condition labels, unique nonempty gene IDs, finite nonnegative counts and positive sample
   totals. Require an exact match between count sample columns and design sample IDs, and
   reorder metadata to the count columns. Stop with the actual error if validation fails.
   Retain all six samples, with no automatic outlier removal.
3. Compute library totals over all genes. Convert counts to counts per million (CPM) by
   dividing each column by its total and multiplying by 1,000,000. Retain genes with CPM
   >= 1 in at least 3 samples. Transform retained CPM with log2(CPM + 1), then remove genes
   with zero variance across samples. Preserve fractional input counts without rounding.
4. Use all retained variable genes, without selecting genes by condition or differential
   expression. Transpose to samples by genes, mean-centre each gene across samples, and
   perform full deterministic SVD (`numpy.linalg.svd`, `full_matrices=False`). Do not scale
   genes to unit variance, correct batches or regress out condition. Require at least two
   nonzero principal components; otherwise stop. Sample scores are U times singular values;
   explained variance ratios are squared singular values divided by their sum.
5. Plot PC1 against PC2 with untreated in blue (#0072B2) and treated in orange (#D55E00).
   Label each point with sample_id, include a condition legend, and label axes with percent
   variance explained. Save a 7 by 5 inch PNG at 300 dpi and a vector PDF. PCA signs are
   arbitrary and do not affect sample relationships.
6. Export scores for all components with sample_id and condition, and a variance table with
   component, eigenvalue (singular value squared divided by n_samples - 1), explained variance
   ratio and cumulative ratio. Write a brief Markdown report documenting input paths and
   SHA-256 hashes, package versions, sample counts by condition, gene counts before and after
   filtering, normalization, PCA parameters, and PC1/PC2 variance percentages. Limit the
   report to this descriptive PCA; perform no significance tests or biological inference.
7. On successful execution, run the stage 03 `verify` helper to check the declared outputs
   and register completion, then append its returned history entry as required by the contract.

